  "reason": "The records collectively make the result plausibly reconstructible. R1, R17, and especially R19 establish SPS near 1000–1050 °C as an effective consolidation treatment for closely related ball-milled, transition-metal HEAs, producing dense or fine-grained high-hardness bulk material. R3 and R13 show that SPS temperature controls diffusion, oxide/secondary-phase precipitation, density, and passivation in mechanically alloyed BCC refractory HEAs. R2, R6, R9, and R11 independently connect dense, uniform oxide/passive films with restricted oxygen or ion penetration and improved oxidation and corrosion resistance, while R14 shows that sufficient temperature-dependent kinetics are needed to form a continuous diffusion barrier. An expert could therefore propose SPS around 1000 °C for the MgAlTiVFeCo powder and expect densification plus oxide-mediated passivation, although the exact AlV2O4, FeAl2O4, and FeTiO3 phase identities and precise optimum properties are not supplied by the earlier records."
